        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 22, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -2, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 3, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["trunc", "round"]}
      ],
      "family": "pipelined",
      "budget_share": 0.45
    },
    {
      "why": "Same 1 result/cycle throughput, but registers only every m stages, so it should give the smallest LUT+FF designs (the min-area corner the objective and the 4000 HV ref care about). The cost is a longer combinational path (lower Fmax) and latency ceil(N/m)+2, which eats into the 0.44 us batch budget, so m is kept moderate (2..6) to keep Fmax comfortably above the ~85-110 MHz implied by (latency+31)/0.44us. This is where the area/accuracy knee most likely lives.",
