{
  "rationale": "Feasible families are pipelined and pipelined_m only. iterative/unrolled_k are ruled out analytically by the system constraint: a 32-request burst must finish in 0.44 us, so throughput must be ~>=73 MSPS. iterative needs Fmax >= 32*(N+3)/0.44us (>=509 MHz at N=4) and unrolled_k needs >=291 MHz even at its best case (ceil(N/k)=1, i.e. N<=k=8, which only gives ~2^-8 accuracy) — neither is reachable, so add_family would waste budget. The current front is narrow in parameter space: data_width is only 21..22 (registry 8..28), and accuracy_bits spans 13.7..17.2 while the HV reference is 12 and the datapath can clearly go higher (data_width up to 28, n_iter up to 30). The cheap end (data_width 18..20) is also unmapped on the front even though pipelined_m was feasible down to data_width=18, so cheaper feasible designs may exist below luts_plus_ffs=1348. HV is dominated by the mid-front segments and by the uncovered region between the front and the ref point (4000, 12) on both axes, so the highest-value action is to broaden the front across the full ranges of the two families that actually appear on it, seeded with the current 9 designs.",
  "next_plan": {
    "rationale": "Map the full Pareto front over pipelined and pipelined_m (full registry ranges, seeded with the current front) to cover the unmapped cheap end (data_width 18..20), the low-accuracy region (12..13.7 bits) and the high-accuracy region (>17.2 bits) before refining.",
