{"decision": "refine", "next_plan": {"families": [{"budget_share": 0.7, "family": "pipelined_m", "ranges": [{"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 6, "low": 2, "param": "m"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 22, "low": 14, "param": "data_width"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 20, "low": 13, "param": "n_iter"}] , "why": "cheapest family (min feasible luts_plus_ffs=1348 at dW=21/N=15/m=4); push data_width down toward the output-quantisation floor (~dW14 for 2^-12) to cut area and raise Fmax"}, {"budget_share": 0.3, "family": "pipelined_m", "ranges": [{"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 22, "low": 14, "param": "data_width"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 20, "low": 13, "param": "n_iter"}], "why": "secondary: pipelined (1/cycle, highest Fmax seen 282 MSPS) at the same low-width band, in case a 1/cycle design with more batch margin is needed for L2"}, {"budget_share": 0.0, "family": "pipelined", "ranges": [{"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": -2, "param": "angle_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 3, "low": 0, "param": "frac_guard"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 22, "low": 14, "param": "data_width"}, {"choices": ["trunc", "round"], "high": 20, "low": 13, "param": "n_iter"}], "why": "placeholder"}] , "rationale": "Do NOT add iterative/unrolled_k. The system issues a 32-request burst per 1us tick and requires sys_p99_batch_us<=0.44 (best seen 0.154) — i.e. ~73 results/us from one shared unit. Non-pipelined families give 1 result per ceil(N/k)+3 (or N+3) cycles, so at the N>=13-15 needed for the 2^-12 error floor they would need Fmax>=73*(N+3) ~ 1.2-2.6 GHz (iterative) or >=73*4-6 cycles ~ 300-450 MHz (unrolled_k) — unattainable on Artix-7, and these are only optimistic L1 bounds. Only the 1-result/cycle families (already on the front) can carry the burst. Accuracy is nowhere near binding (best 4.62e-8 vs 2^-12), area is: the front's cheap corner is 1348 luts+ffs at dW=21, while the registry allows dW down to 8 and per-family feasible sampling only reached dW=18. Reducing data_width lowers luts_plus_ffs (the selection objective) AND raises Fmax, which buys margin on the batch bound that the current cheapest design (93.6 MSPS -> ~0.35-0.4us at L1) only just satisfies — directly de-risking the L2 re-selection. That is the highest-value region; keep the last round for the reserved full-front mapping."} 



