  "rationale": "Round 2 of 4, 200/400 evals used. The front already spans luts_plus_ffs 1348..5385 against HV ref 4000 and accuracy 13.7..24.4 against ref 12, so global coverage is good and the remaining gain is in (a) the cheap corner that the selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) actually picks and (b) L2 robustness. Evidence: accuracy is far from binding (best 4.62e-08 vs 2^-12, 20% violate but never the good designs), throughput never binds (0% violate), but sys_p99_batch_us is close (best 0.154 vs 0.44) and is only an optimistic L1 bound — the note warns cheap designs that just pass L1 may be lost at L2. The cheapest front design (pipelined_m dW=21/N=15/m=4, 1348 luts+ffs) runs at 93.6 MSPS; a smaller datapath is both cheaper and faster, so probing dW 14..22 buys area and batch margin at once. I am NOT adding iterative/unrolled_k: they emit ≤1 result per ceil(N/k)+3 (or N+3) cycles, so at the N≥13 needed for 2^-12 they would need Fmax ≳ 73*(cycles/result) ≈ 300 MHz (unrolled_k) to >1 GHz (iterative) just to place 32 results in 0.44us — unreachable, and only against the optimistic bound. Round 3 explores the low-width region; round 4 stays reserved for the full-front mapping over pipelined/pipelined_m."}

{
  "decision": "add_family",
  "rationale": "The front is already well-covered on both objectives (luts_plus_ffs 1139..5385 vs HV ref 4000; accuracy_bits 12.3..24.4 vs HV ref 12), so map_front is not indicated by the 'front covers only a small part of an objective's range' rule, and the +6.8% HV gain shows it is still improving, so stop is premature. The binding gap is that only pipelined/pipelined_m have been searched (300 evals, 228 of them pipelined_m), while iterative and unrolled_k are untouched. Since the objective is min luts_plus_ffs and the current cheapest feasible point is 1139 (pipelined_m, W=17/N=14/ag=1/fg=2/trunc/m=4), the shared-datapath families are the only untested place a cheaper design could hide. Note the effective system requirement is stricter than the stated throughput_msps>=32: 32 requests inside 0.44 us needs ~73 MSPS, and the cheapest front point at 93.6 MSPS already sits at 0.342 us, so any new family must clear that bar (iterative's N+3 cycles/result likely cannot, unrolled_k with large k can).",
